-- md --
Usage: rex ls \[flags\]

List sessions, newest state first. -wide adds start and end times and the resume id.

#### Flags

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `-n int` | lines (default 5) |
| `-socket path` | daemon socket path (default $XDG\_RUNTIME\_DIR/rex.sock, else \~/.cache/rex/rex.sock) |
| `-state string` | filter by state |
| `-timeout wait` | max wait time |
| `-wide` | add columns |

#### Output

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `-o, --output FORMAT` | text, txt, md, json, agent |
| `--agent` | one line per record, no color, no prompts |
| `--no-color` | never emit ANSI color |
| `-json` | legacy JSON shape (prefer -o json) |

#### Example

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `rex ls -state needs_input` |  |
